"Collision kerma of primary photons: K_col = Φ hν (μ_en/ρ) e^(−μz) with NIST liquid water μ/ρ and μ_en/ρ (Hubbell and Seltzer), log–log interpolated; broad parallel beam, primary photons only.",
"Absorbed dose: D(z) = ∫ K_col(z − x) G(x) dx. G comes from the Klein–Nishina electron spectrum (dσ/dT, Attix eq. {#} form) and electron angle (cot θ_e = ({#} + k) tan(θ/{#})); each electron goes straight for its ESTAR CSDA range in water and leaves its ESTAR collision stopping power along the path; G is normalized to {#} so the collision kerma is conserved. Compton μ_C with ESTAR collision losses reproduces NIST μ_en/ρ within {#} % at {#} MeV. No multiple scattering, so the shape of the buildup is a sketch (⁶⁰Co: model d_max {#} mm, β {#}).",
"Monte Carlo: the same physics sampled per photon (depth from e^(−μz), a Compton event with probability μ_C/μ, electron energy by inverting the Klein–Nishina distribution), batches of {#} histories, uncertainty = standard deviation of the batch means/√n_batch; the probe readout is linear between the two nearest bin centers, so it compares with the model at the same depth.",
"Chamber: a Farmer type cavity of {#} cm³ (PTW {#}), radius {#} mm, central electrode radius {#} mm (typical), Boag's equivalent gap {#} mm. Air density from the ideal gas law (dry air, {#} g/mol). Recombination: pulsed f = ln({#} + u)/u, u = α n₀ d²/((k₁ + k₂)V), and continuous f = {#}/({#} + m² d⁴ q/(6V²)) (Boag {#}), with α = {#} × {#}⁻¹² m³/s, k₁ = {#} × {#}⁻⁴, k₂ = {#} × {#}⁻⁴ m²/(V s) (Fenwick and Kumar {#}). Initial recombination and charge multiplication are left out. The polarity effect (+{#} % in protons, +{#} % in ⁶⁰Co) and the reading noise ({#} %) are simulated.",
"TRS-{#} ({#}) key data: proton s_w,air = {#} − {#} × {#}⁻⁵ R_res + {#} × {#}⁻³/R_res, W_air = {#} eV for protons and {#} eV for ⁶⁰Co, s_w,air(⁶⁰Co) = {#}, p_Q = {#} in protons, p_Co = {#} (PTW {#}), {#} (NE {#}), {#} (FC65-G) (as tabulated by Burigo and Greilich {#}); two voltage coefficients for pulsed radiation. ICRU {#} W_air = {#} eV for protons is a Lab option. Reference depth for scanned layers from TRS-{#} Rev. {#} Table {#} ({#} g/cm² when R_res ≥ {#} g/cm², else {#} g/cm²); R_p is the PSTAR CSDA range, a stated simplification.",
"The simulated chamber is built from the same formulas, so the protocol closes: with exact Boag k_s the calculated dose equals the delivered dose to {#} part in {#}⁵; with the TRS-{#} two voltage polynomial, to about {#} % at {#} mGy per pulse. N_D,w (simulated certificate) = s_w,air p_Co W_air/(ρ_air V), {#} × {#}⁷ Gy/C ({#} nC/Gy) for the PTW {#} against PTW's nominal {#} nC/Gy.",
